  "sourceUrl": "https://techspecs.ui.com/unifi/switching/us-48",
  "notes": "The Gen1 Standard 48 spec table prints no PoE row at all: Port Layout \"1 GbE RJ45 48 (1G/100M/10M), 1G SFP 2 (1G), 10G SFP+ 2 (10G/1G)\", Power Method \"Universal input, 100-240V AC, 50/60 Hz\" - no per-port wattage, no budget, no PoE standard. The PoE members of the Gen1 family are separate models carrying their own budgets (us-48-500w.json 500 W, us-48-750w.json 750 W), so the silence is the product decision, not a blank field. Without `poeIn: false` on its 48 copper sockets `isPoePd()` in `engine/media.js` matched `unifi` in the label and inferred a 12.95 W 802.3af draw on every one - **621.6 W** asked of whatever PSE the lab cabled it to. Same correction as the non-PoE Switch Pro and Pro Max rows (PR #1712, PR #1715)."
